sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The competency-ratchet model predicts, and it is the case, that there are no known mutant planarian strains with abnormal morphologies (unlike flies or mice), explains the difficulty of making transgenic planaria, and the only known permanent abnormal planarian lines (two-headed and randomized 1- vs 2-head forms) arose from bioelectric rather than genetic change.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The competency ratchet predicts no planarian mutant strains with abnormal morphology";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “An evolutionary intelligence ratchet”. Scope: Planarians compared with Drosophila, mice and other model organisms"
}
